  "description": "Tamp wrapper for Cisco's mcp-scanner. Scans MCP servers (remote, static tool manifest, or config file) for tool-poisoning / prompt-injection / credential-harvesting and related threats, and normalises the scanner's JSON into SARIF 2.1.0 so MCP findings flow through the Tamp security chain (merge, dedup, DefectDojo/Dependency-Track push, tamp-findings). Offline analyzers (yara, readiness, prompt_defense) by default; LLM/vendor analyzers are opt-in. Findings are about advertised tools, not files — they carry SARIF logicalLocations, not synthesised paths. Noisy by nature: intended as nightly, non-blocking evidence, not a per-push gate. Requires the Cisco mcp-scanner CLI on the machine that runs the scan.",
  "id": "Tamp.McpScanner",
  "isPrerelease": false,
